# CHAPTER 3 — PROBLEM STATEMENT

Investigating a mystery often involves handling multiple suspects, clues, documents and pieces of evidence.

When this information is managed manually, it becomes difficult to organise evidence, track investigation progress and identify relationships between different pieces of information.

There is a need for a centralised digital platform that provides structured investigation management and AI-assisted mystery generation.

MysteryRoom addresses this requirement by providing an interactive environment for creating, managing and solving mystery cases.

# CHAPTER 4 — PROJECT OBJECTIVES

The major objectives are:

- Develop a full-stack AI investigation application.
- Create interactive mystery cases.
- Organise suspects and clues.
- Integrate a generative AI model.
- Manage investigation progress.
- Provide hints and accusation functionality.
- Implement an automated scoring mechanism.
- Store investigation data in a database.
- Implement authentication and protected access.
- Develop a responsive and user-friendly interface.
- Prepare the application for deployment.

# CHAPTER 5 — EXISTING SYSTEM

In a conventional investigation or mystery-solving process, evidence is often maintained using separate documents, notes or manually organised information.

This creates several limitations:

- Evidence is difficult to organise centrally.
- Suspect information may become disconnected from clues.
- Investigation progress is difficult to track.
- Manual analysis can be time-consuming.
- There is no integrated scoring mechanism.
- Information may be difficult to retrieve later.

# CHAPTER 6 — PROPOSED SYSTEM

MysteryRoom provides a centralised AI-powered investigation environment.

The proposed system integrates frontend interfaces, backend APIs, database services and generative AI.

Users can create and investigate mystery cases through a structured interface.

The backend handles the investigation logic and protects hidden solutions and undiscovered clue contents.

The system also supports database persistence and authentication.

